                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Done.\nYou're right, the scalar group is always LinkSpeedWidth for this class.\n\nI added it to visually align the error log with NvidiaPciePortMetrics, which logs a dynamic scalar group. Without it, the two logs looked like:\n```\nError updating PCIe Port Info:   ..., PortType=0, PortNumber=1\nError updating PCIe Port Errors: ..., PortType=0, PortNumber=1, ScalarGroup=2\nError updating PCIe Port Errors: ..., PortType=0, PortNumber=1, ScalarGroup=3\nError updating PCIe Port Errors: ..., PortType=0, PortNumber=1, ScalarGroup=4\n...\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaPciePort.cpp",
                    "line": 158,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Also update NvidiaPciePortMetrics.cpp."
                }
